{"type_of":"article","id":4934411,"title":"Why our MCP server stopped trusting localhost by default","description":"A local relay can make a remote request look local. A Python reconstruction shows the mistake behind a change in aimarket-mcp 0.6.4.","readable_publish_date":"Oct 28","slug":"why-our-mcp-server-stopped-trusting-localhost-by-default-26jm","path":"/alexar76/why-our-mcp-server-stopped-trusting-localhost-by-default-26jm","url":"https://dev.to/alexar76/why-our-mcp-server-stopped-trusting-localhost-by-default-26jm","comments_count":0,"public_reactions_count":1,"collection_id":null,"published_timestamp":"2026-10-28T12:01:47Z","language":"en","subforem_id":1,"ai_disclosure_level":"fully_autonomous","ai_disclosure_label":"Fully Autonomous","positive_reactions_count":1,"cover_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=1000,height=420,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmodelmarket.dev%2Fblog%2Fmedia%2Flocalhost-auth-2026-10-28%2F01-cover.png","social_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=1200,height=627,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmodelmarket.dev%2Fblog%2Fmedia%2Flocalhost-auth-2026-10-28%2F01-cover.png","canonical_url":"https://dev.to/alexar76/why-our-mcp-server-stopped-trusting-localhost-by-default-26jm","created_at":"2026-10-28T12:01:09Z","edited_at":"2026-10-28T12:03:17Z","crossposted_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-28T12:01:47Z","last_comment_at":"2026-10-28T12:01:47Z","reading_time_minutes":6,"tag_list":"mcp, security, python, opensource","tags":["mcp","security","python","opensource"],"body_html":"\u003cp\u003eThe backend sees \u003ccode\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/code\u003e. The authorization code decides that the request belongs to the person running the server.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA local reverse proxy breaks that inference. Its connection to the backend is local even when the request that caused it came from somewhere else.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe maintain AIMarket MCP Gateway. In version 0.6.3, our keyless HTTP path tried to identify a local caller using its socket and operating-system user. Vulnetix pointed out the remaining gap: a proxy running as that same user could satisfy those checks. If the Linux socket tables were unavailable, the ownership check also returned success.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIn \u003ca href=\"https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-mcp/0.6.4/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e0.6.4, released on 28 October\u003c/a\u003e, ordinary HTTP RPC requests without a configured key are refused by default, including direct loopback requests. Here is the small reconstruction that makes the reason visible.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"the-backend-sees-the-last-connection\" href=\"#the-backend-sees-the-last-connection\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  The backend sees the last connection\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eConsider a development tool bound to loopback, with a relay on the same machine:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F51kk1wfyoliib6f4bin8.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F51kk1wfyoliib6f4bin8.png\" alt=\"A remote caller reaches a local relay, which opens a new loopback connection to the backend. A direct local client also reaches the backend from loopback.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"427\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eDeployment model. The relay needs no special ability to forge an address: it opens a new connection. The executable example below keeps every listener and client on loopback.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe backend can inspect its TCP peer. In Python's \u003ccode\u003eBaseHTTPRequestHandler\u003c/code\u003e, that address is available through \u003ca href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/http.server.html#http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler.client_address\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003eclient_address\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA deliberately simplified version of the mistake is:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight python\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eallowed\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eip_address\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eclient_address\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]).\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eis_loopback\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003eThat condition describes the connection. Once it authorizes a private operation, a relay can carry someone else's request through it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOur old code had more conditions than this one line: loopback Host and peer checks, browser Origin checks, forwarding-header rejection, and socket ownership. Those checks cover particular paths. They still cannot distinguish a direct client from an arbitrary relay owned by the same user.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA relay can construct the upstream Host, omit Origin and forwarding headers, and open the backend socket under its own user. A process name does not establish who requested the operation either.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"eight-requests-with-an-ordinary-http-relay\" href=\"#eight-requests-with-an-ordinary-http-relay\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  Eight requests with an ordinary HTTP relay\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eI made a small standard-library example with two interchangeable backend policies:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAccept any loopback peer.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRequire the expected Bearer credential.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe relay forwards a fixed \u003ccode\u003e/private\u003c/code\u003e request to a fixed loopback target. It copies an Authorization header only when the client supplied one. It never supplies its own backend credential to anonymous callers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eEvery listener uses \u003ccode\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/code\u003e and an automatically allocated port. The key is generated in memory for this run and never printed. Running the example produced:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F34liwgx0ne608zs7ebes.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F34liwgx0ne608zs7ebes.png\" alt=\"Eight requests in the local reconstruction: the peer-only gate accepts two requests without keys. The Bearer gate rejects missing and wrong keys on both paths, and accepts the valid key on both paths. Every backend peer address is 127.0.0.1.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"511\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eThese are results from the educational HTTP reconstruction. It does not run the MCP package or reproduce a remote attack against a deployment.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe backend peer \u003cstrong\u003eaddress\u003c/strong\u003e remains \u003ccode\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/code\u003e in all eight requests. Changing the authorization policy changes which requests succeed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"reproduce-it-locally\" href=\"#reproduce-it-locally\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  Reproduce it locally\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eSave the following as \u003ccode\u003elocalhost_auth_demo.py\u003c/code\u003e and run \u003ccode\u003epython3 localhost_auth_demo.py\u003c/code\u003e. It uses Python 3.9 or later, needs no packages, serves no files and contacts no external host. Assertions check all eight responses, and both servers shut down after each policy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"complete-python-reconstruction\" href=\"#complete-python-reconstruction\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  Complete Python reconstruction\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight js-code-highlight\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"highlight python\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\"\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eEducational HTTP reconstruction; fixed localhost targets, no MCP dependency.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\"\"\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econtextlib\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econtextmanager\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ehmac\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecompare_digest\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ehttp.client\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eHTTPConnection\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ehttp.server\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eBaseHTTPRequestHandler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eThreadingHTTPServer\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eipaddress\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eip_address\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esecrets\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003efrom\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethreading\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kn\"\u003eimport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eThread\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\n\u003cspan class=\"nd\"\u003e@contextmanager\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eserve\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ehandler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserver\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003eThreadingHTTPServer\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e((\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ehandler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethread\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003eThread\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etarget\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserver\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserve_forever\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edaemon\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"bp\"\u003eTrue\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethread\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003estart\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003etry\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eyield\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserver\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserver_port\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efinally\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserver\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eshutdown\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserver\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eserver_close\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethread\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ejoin\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etimeout\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003eQuietHandler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eBaseHTTPRequestHandler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003elog_message\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eargs\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003epass\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# No request or credential logging in this demonstration.\n\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ebackend_handler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequire_key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003eBackend\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eQuietHandler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003edo_GET\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epath\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e!=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/private\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esend_error\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e404\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epeer\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eclient_address\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esupplied\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eget\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eAuthorization\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e).\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eencode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eutf-8\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eaccepted\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ecompare_digest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esupplied\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sa\"\u003ef\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eBearer \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eencode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eascii\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e))\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequire_key\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eip_address\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epeer\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e).\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eis_loopback\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epayload\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003edumps\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e({\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eaccepted\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eaccepted\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003epeer\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epeer\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}).\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eencode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esend_response\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e200\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eaccepted\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e401\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esend_header\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eContent-Type\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eapplication/json\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esend_header\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eContent-Length\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003estr\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003elen\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epayload\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)))\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eend_headers\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ewfile\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ewrite\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epayload\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eBackend\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003erelay_handler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eupstream_port\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eclass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003eRelay\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eQuietHandler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003edo_GET\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Fixed upstream/path; no URL supplied by the caller.\n\u003c/span\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{}\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eAuthorization\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eAuthorization\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eAuthorization\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003eHTTPConnection\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eupstream_port\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etimeout\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003etry\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econn\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003erequest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eGET\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/private\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresponse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econn\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003egetresponse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epayload\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresponse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eread\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esend_response\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresponse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003estatus\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esend_header\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eContent-Type\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eapplication/json\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003esend_header\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eContent-Length\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003estr\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003elen\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epayload\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)))\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eend_headers\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eself\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ewfile\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ewrite\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epayload\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efinally\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econn\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eclose\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eRelay\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003erequest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eport\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"bp\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e):\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nc\"\u003eHTTPConnection\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eport\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etimeout\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003etry\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eAuthorization\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sa\"\u003ef\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eBearer \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"si\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003eis\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003enot\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"bp\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{}\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econn\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003erequest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eGET\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/private\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eheaders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresponse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econn\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003egetresponse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresponse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003estatus\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eloads\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresponse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eread\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e())\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efinally\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econn\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eclose\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003edef\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003emain\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e():\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esecrets\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003etoken_urlsafe\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e32\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresults\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[]\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003emode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequire_key\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e((\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003epeer-only\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"bp\"\u003eFalse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003ebearer\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"bp\"\u003eTrue\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)):\u003c/span\u003e\n        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ewith\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eserve\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003ebackend_handler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequire_key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e))\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eas\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebackend\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ewith\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eserve\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003erelay_handler\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebackend\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e))\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eas\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erelay\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecases\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003edirect, no key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebackend\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"bp\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e401\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequire_key\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e200\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e\n                         \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003erelay, no key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erelay\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"bp\"\u003eNone\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e401\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequire_key\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e200\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)]\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequire_key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n                    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecases\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e+=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003edirect, wrong key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebackend\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003ewrong-demo-key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e401\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e\n                              \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003erelay, wrong key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erelay\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003ewrong-demo-key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e401\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e\n                              \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003edirect, valid key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebackend\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e200\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e\n                              \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003erelay, valid key\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erelay\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e200\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)]\u003c/span\u003e\n                \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efor\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003elabel\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eport\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecredential\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eexpected\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ow\"\u003ein\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecases\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n                    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003estatus\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebody\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003erequest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eport\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecredential\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n                    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003estatus\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e==\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eexpected\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003emode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003elabel\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003estatus\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n                    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebody\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003epeer\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e==\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e127.0.0.1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebody\u003c/span\u003e\n                    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eassert\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebody\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eaccepted\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e==\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003estatus\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e==\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e200\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebody\u003c/span\u003e\n                    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresults\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eappend\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e({\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003egate\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003emode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003epath\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003elabel\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n                                    \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003estatus\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003estatus\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003ebackend_peer\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebody\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003epeer\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]})\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003eprint\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003edumps\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e({\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003escope\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eeducational HTTP reconstruction; all listeners and clients use IPv4 loopback\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n                      \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003echecks\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003elen\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresults\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e),\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eresults\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eresults\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eindent\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e))\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\n\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e__name__\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e==\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e__main__\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sh\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"nf\"\u003emain\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel js-actions-panel\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-on\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eEnter fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M16 3h6v6h-2V5h-4V3zM2 3h6v2H4v4H2V3zm18 16v-4h2v6h-6v-2h4zM4 19h4v2H2v-6h2v4z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n    \u003csvg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" class=\"highlight-action crayons-icon highlight-action--fullscreen-off\"\u003e\u003ctitle\u003eExit fullscreen mode\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cpath d=\"M18 7h4v2h-6V3h2v4zM8 9H2V7h4V3h2v6zm10 8v4h-2v-6h6v2h-4zM8 15v6H6v-4H2v-2h6z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n\u003c/svg\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe credential check in the example uses \u003ca href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/hmac.html#hmac.compare_digest\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003ecompare_digest\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. That makes the comparison appropriate for a secret; it does not turn this teaching server into a production authentication system. Python's own documentation describes the limits of \u003ccode\u003ehttp.server\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"what-we-changed-in-the-real-package\" href=\"#what-we-changed-in-the-real-package\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  What we changed in the real package\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href=\"https://pypi.org/pypi/aimarket-mcp/0.6.4/json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003epublished 0.6.4 wheel\u003c/a\u003e changes the default for the HTTP RPC POST handler:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"table-wrapper-paragraph\"\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eConfiguration\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eRPC behavior\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003eAIMARKET_MCP_KEY\u003c/code\u003e set\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eRequire the matching Bearer credential.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eNo key, ordinary defaults\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eRefuse the RPC request, including on loopback.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003eAIMARKET_MCP_LOCAL_RELAY=1\u003c/code\u003e, no key\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eIn development mode, explicitly trust eligible local TCP callers, including relays owned by the server's user. Other local checks still apply.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eNo Linux socket tables in that opt-in mode\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAlso require \u003ccode\u003eAIMARKET_MCP_LOCAL_UNVERIFIED=1\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003eAIMARKET_MCP_PUBLIC=1\u003c/code\u003e, no key\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eExplicitly allow anonymous RPC.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe operator supplies the key \u003cstrong\u003ebefore starting the process\u003c/strong\u003e. The package does not generate it automatically. Public mode also applies in production; it is a deliberate choice. A configured key takes precedence over public mode.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThis change concerns HTTP RPC authorization. \u003ccode\u003e/health\u003c/code\u003e remains public, and stdio does not acquire an HTTP key requirement.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Vulnetix/advisory-database/blob/main/cvelistv5/VULN-PYPI/2026/0xxx/GCVE-110-VULN-PYPI-2026-000640.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eVulnetix record\u003c/a\u003e was still published without a fixed version listed when checked on 28 October. We inspected both published wheels and confirmed the code change; we are not claiming the researcher has verified 0.6.4 or closed the record.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e\n  \u003ca name=\"where-to-put-the-authorization-decision\" href=\"#where-to-put-the-authorization-decision\"\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n  Where to put the authorization decision\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eKeep a private backend on loopback when that fits the deployment. Then decide explicitly which component authenticates each request. A backend credential, a properly configured authenticating proxy, or an appropriately protected local IPC channel can enforce the intended policy. Each arrangement has its own trust assumptions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIf a proxy authenticates users and then presents one shared backend credential, that proxy holds the authorization boundary. Anyone who can use that forwarding path must pass its access checks. Otherwise the credential simply carries the anonymous caller further.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eForwarded address headers help recover client addresses only when they come from a configured trusted proxy. The resulting address still needs an authorization policy. Browser Origin checks address another part of the problem; arbitrary HTTP clients can construct their own headers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA Bearer credential also has a precise limit: possession grants access. It does not identify a human by itself, and it will not protect a secret from a compromised process that can read that secret. Protect the credential, avoid logging it, and keep privileges narrow. For an interoperable MCP authorization deployment, use the protocol's \u003ca href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/latest/basic/authorization\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eauthorization specification\u003c/a\u003e rather than treating this small example as an OAuth implementation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe practical test I would add to any local HTTP tool is straightforward: put the relay you actually deploy in front of it, send a request without a credential, and assert that the private operation is refused. Keep that test when changing launchers, tunnels or proxy configuration.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eDisclosure: we build AIMarket MCP Gateway, HISTOR and WARDEN. AI assistance was used for the code, writing and cover illustration. The two explanatory figures were rendered from code; the results figure reads the saved output of the local reconstruction. The cover is an editorial metaphor.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","body_markdown":"The backend sees `127.0.0.1`. The authorization code decides that the request belongs to the person running the server.\n\nA local reverse proxy breaks that inference. Its connection to the backend is local even when the request that caused it came from somewhere else.\n\nWe maintain AIMarket MCP Gateway. In version 0.6.3, our keyless HTTP path tried to identify a local caller using its socket and operating-system user. Vulnetix pointed out the remaining gap: a proxy running as that same user could satisfy those checks. If the Linux socket tables were unavailable, the ownership check also returned success.\n\nIn [0.6.4, released on 28 October](https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-mcp/0.6.4/), ordinary HTTP RPC requests without a configured key are refused by default, including direct loopback requests. Here is the small reconstruction that makes the reason visible.\n\n## The backend sees the last connection\n\nConsider a development tool bound to loopback, with a relay on the same machine:\n\n![A remote caller reaches a local relay, which opens a new loopback connection to the backend. A direct local client also reaches the backend from loopback.](https://modelmarket.dev/blog/media/localhost-auth-2026-10-28/02-last-hop.png)\n\n*Deployment model. The relay needs no special ability to forge an address: it opens a new connection. The executable example below keeps every listener and client on loopback.*\n\nThe backend can inspect its TCP peer. In Python's `BaseHTTPRequestHandler`, that address is available through [`client_address`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/http.server.html#http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler.client_address).\n\nA deliberately simplified version of the mistake is:\n\n```python\nallowed = ip_address(self.client_address[0]).is_loopback\n```\n\nThat condition describes the connection. Once it authorizes a private operation, a relay can carry someone else's request through it.\n\nOur old code had more conditions than this one line: loopback Host and peer checks, browser Origin checks, forwarding-header rejection, and socket ownership. Those checks cover particular paths. They still cannot distinguish a direct client from an arbitrary relay owned by the same user.\n\nA relay can construct the upstream Host, omit Origin and forwarding headers, and open the backend socket under its own user. A process name does not establish who requested the operation either.\n\n## Eight requests with an ordinary HTTP relay\n\nI made a small standard-library example with two interchangeable backend policies:\n\n1. Accept any loopback peer.\n2. Require the expected Bearer credential.\n\nThe relay forwards a fixed `/private` request to a fixed loopback target. It copies an Authorization header only when the client supplied one. It never supplies its own backend credential to anonymous callers.\n\nEvery listener uses `127.0.0.1` and an automatically allocated port. The key is generated in memory for this run and never printed. Running the example produced:\n\n![Eight requests in the local reconstruction: the peer-only gate accepts two requests without keys. The Bearer gate rejects missing and wrong keys on both paths, and accepts the valid key on both paths. Every backend peer address is 127.0.0.1.](https://modelmarket.dev/blog/media/localhost-auth-2026-10-28/03-demo-results.png)\n\n*These are results from the educational HTTP reconstruction. It does not run the MCP package or reproduce a remote attack against a deployment.*\n\nThe backend peer **address** remains `127.0.0.1` in all eight requests. Changing the authorization policy changes which requests succeed.\n\n## Reproduce it locally\n\nSave the following as `localhost_auth_demo.py` and run `python3 localhost_auth_demo.py`. It uses Python 3.9 or later, needs no packages, serves no files and contacts no external host. Assertions check all eight responses, and both servers shut down after each policy.\n\n### Complete Python reconstruction\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Educational HTTP reconstruction; fixed localhost targets, no MCP dependency.\"\"\"\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nfrom hmac import compare_digest\nfrom http.client import HTTPConnection\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\nfrom ipaddress import ip_address\nimport json\nimport secrets\nfrom threading import Thread\n\n\n@contextmanager\ndef serve(handler):\n    server = ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", 0), handler)\n    thread = Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True)\n    thread.start()\n    try:\n        yield server.server_port\n    finally:\n        server.shutdown()\n        server.server_close()\n        thread.join(timeout=2)\n\n\nclass QuietHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self, *args):\n        pass  # No request or credential logging in this demonstration.\n\n\ndef backend_handler(require_key, key):\n    class Backend(QuietHandler):\n        def do_GET(self):\n            if self.path != \"/private\":\n                self.send_error(404)\n                return\n            peer = self.client_address[0]\n            supplied = self.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\").encode(\"utf-8\")\n            accepted = (\n                compare_digest(supplied, f\"Bearer {key}\".encode(\"ascii\"))\n                if require_key else ip_address(peer).is_loopback\n            )\n            payload = json.dumps({\"accepted\": accepted, \"peer\": peer}).encode()\n            self.send_response(200 if accepted else 401)\n            self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n            self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(payload)))\n            self.end_headers()\n            self.wfile.write(payload)\n    return Backend\n\n\ndef relay_handler(upstream_port):\n    class Relay(QuietHandler):\n        def do_GET(self):\n            # Fixed upstream/path; no URL supplied by the caller.\n            headers = {}\n            if \"Authorization\" in self.headers:\n                headers[\"Authorization\"] = self.headers[\"Authorization\"]\n            conn = HTTPConnection(\"127.0.0.1\", upstream_port, timeout=3)\n            try:\n                conn.request(\"GET\", \"/private\", headers=headers)\n                response = conn.getresponse()\n                payload = response.read()\n                self.send_response(response.status)\n                self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n                self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(payload)))\n                self.end_headers()\n                self.wfile.write(payload)\n            finally:\n                conn.close()\n    return Relay\n\n\ndef request(port, key=None):\n    conn = HTTPConnection(\"127.0.0.1\", port, timeout=3)\n    try:\n        headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {key}\"} if key is not None else {}\n        conn.request(\"GET\", \"/private\", headers=headers)\n        response = conn.getresponse()\n        return response.status, json.loads(response.read())\n    finally:\n        conn.close()\n\n\ndef main():\n    key = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n    results = []\n    for mode, require_key in ((\"peer-only\", False), (\"bearer\", True)):\n        with serve(backend_handler(require_key, key)) as backend:\n            with serve(relay_handler(backend)) as relay:\n                cases = [(\"direct, no key\", backend, None, 401 if require_key else 200),\n                         (\"relay, no key\", relay, None, 401 if require_key else 200)]\n                if require_key:\n                    cases += [(\"direct, wrong key\", backend, \"wrong-demo-key\", 401),\n                              (\"relay, wrong key\", relay, \"wrong-demo-key\", 401),\n                              (\"direct, valid key\", backend, key, 200),\n                              (\"relay, valid key\", relay, key, 200)]\n                for label, port, credential, expected in cases:\n                    status, body = request(port, credential)\n                    assert status == expected, (mode, label, status)\n                    assert body[\"peer\"] == \"127.0.0.1\", body\n                    assert body[\"accepted\"] == (status == 200), body\n                    results.append({\"gate\": mode, \"path\": label,\n                                    \"status\": status, \"backend_peer\": body[\"peer\"]})\n    print(json.dumps({\"scope\": \"educational HTTP reconstruction; all listeners and clients use IPv4 loopback\",\n                      \"checks\": len(results), \"results\": results}, indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n\nThe credential check in the example uses [`compare_digest`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/hmac.html#hmac.compare_digest). That makes the comparison appropriate for a secret; it does not turn this teaching server into a production authentication system. Python's own documentation describes the limits of `http.server`.\n\n## What we changed in the real package\n\nThe [published 0.6.4 wheel](https://pypi.org/pypi/aimarket-mcp/0.6.4/json) changes the default for the HTTP RPC POST handler:\n\n| Configuration | RPC behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `AIMARKET_MCP_KEY` set | Require the matching Bearer credential. |\n| No key, ordinary defaults | Refuse the RPC request, including on loopback. |\n| `AIMARKET_MCP_LOCAL_RELAY=1`, no key | In development mode, explicitly trust eligible local TCP callers, including relays owned by the server's user. Other local checks still apply. |\n| No Linux socket tables in that opt-in mode | Also require `AIMARKET_MCP_LOCAL_UNVERIFIED=1`. |\n| `AIMARKET_MCP_PUBLIC=1`, no key | Explicitly allow anonymous RPC. |\n\nThe operator supplies the key **before starting the process**. The package does not generate it automatically. Public mode also applies in production; it is a deliberate choice. A configured key takes precedence over public mode.\n\nThis change concerns HTTP RPC authorization. `/health` remains public, and stdio does not acquire an HTTP key requirement.\n\nThe [Vulnetix record](https://github.com/Vulnetix/advisory-database/blob/main/cvelistv5/VULN-PYPI/2026/0xxx/GCVE-110-VULN-PYPI-2026-000640.json) was still published without a fixed version listed when checked on 28 October. We inspected both published wheels and confirmed the code change; we are not claiming the researcher has verified 0.6.4 or closed the record.\n\n## Where to put the authorization decision\n\nKeep a private backend on loopback when that fits the deployment. Then decide explicitly which component authenticates each request. A backend credential, a properly configured authenticating proxy, or an appropriately protected local IPC channel can enforce the intended policy. Each arrangement has its own trust assumptions.\n\nIf a proxy authenticates users and then presents one shared backend credential, that proxy holds the authorization boundary. Anyone who can use that forwarding path must pass its access checks. Otherwise the credential simply carries the anonymous caller further.\n\nForwarded address headers help recover client addresses only when they come from a configured trusted proxy. The resulting address still needs an authorization policy. Browser Origin checks address another part of the problem; arbitrary HTTP clients can construct their own headers.\n\nA Bearer credential also has a precise limit: possession grants access. It does not identify a human by itself, and it will not protect a secret from a compromised process that can read that secret. Protect the credential, avoid logging it, and keep privileges narrow. For an interoperable MCP authorization deployment, use the protocol's [authorization specification](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/latest/basic/authorization) rather than treating this small example as an OAuth implementation.\n\nThe practical test I would add to any local HTTP tool is straightforward: put the relay you actually deploy in front of it, send a request without a credential, and assert that the private operation is refused. Keep that test when changing launchers, tunnels or proxy configuration.\n\n*Disclosure: we build AIMarket MCP Gateway, HISTOR and WARDEN. AI assistance was used for the code, writing and cover illustration. The two explanatory figures were rendered from code; the results figure reads the saved output of the local reconstruction. The cover is an editorial metaphor.*\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"}}